---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  PageContentPlayground,
  PageContentExamples,
} from "../../components/PageContentDemo";
---

<Docs title="Page Content">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Page Content</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    The padded column that holds a page's header and sections. It gives every
    page the same edges and the same space between blocks.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><PageContentPlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Page content usage"
      code={`import { PageContent } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/page-content";
import { PageHeader } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/page-header";

<div className="min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-auto">
  <PageContent>
    <PageHeader title="Usage" description="Credits, and where they go." />
    <WorkspaceCredits />
  </PageContent>
</div>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>PageContent</code> fills the width and never forces its parent wider (<code
        >min-width: 0</code
      >). Padding is 16px on small screens and 24px left and right, 20px top and
      bottom from 640px. Direct children sit 16px apart. Hidden children, such
      as a <code>hidden</code> file input, and children that render nothing add no
      space.
    </p>
    <p>
      It does not scroll. Put it in your own scroll region, usually a <code
        >min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-auto</code
      > column under the app header. It takes every <code>div</code> prop, including
      <code>ref</code> and <code>className</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Compositions</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Scroll region, restoration, and edge bleed"
      code={`// Room under the list for a floating composer
<div role="region" aria-label="Chat list" className="min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto pb-24">
  <PageContent>…</PageContent>
</div>

// Keep the scroller in a ref to save and restore its position
<div ref={scroller} data-scroll-restoration-id="files-library" className="min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto">
  <PageContent>…</PageContent>
</div>

// A rail that scrolls edge to edge on small screens
<nav className="-mx-[var(--sprout-page-content-inline)] px-[var(--sprout-page-content-inline)] overflow-x-auto">…</nav>`}
    />
    <p>
      The current padding is on <code>--sprout-page-content-inline</code> and <code
        >--sprout-page-content-block</code
      >; the gap is <code>--sprout-page-content-gap</code>. Children can read
      these to bleed to the edge. Spacing has zero specificity, so a child's own
      margin class wins.
    </p>
    <PageContentExamples client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      <code>PageContent</code> is a plain <code>div</code> with no role and no motion.
      Give the scroll region a name with <code>role="region"</code> and <code
        >aria-label</code
      > when it is a landmark, and let the keyboard reach it with <code
        >{"tabIndex={0}"}</code
      > when it has no focusable content. The page's <code>h1</code> comes from <code
        >PageHeader</code
      >. Routing and data in these examples are sample code.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
